type: software
title: "KUSAK-INFRA: 11-Month Pre-Registered Quantitative Research and Low-Latency C++20 Execution Engine Archive"
abstract: >-
  Archive of an 11-month (Dec 2025 - Nov 2026) pre-registered quantitative
  research program and the low-latency C++20 / Linux x86-64 execution engine
  built for it. The single-symbol engine for Binance Spot and USD-M Futures
  uses lock-free SPSC rings between pinned threads, a table-driven 14-state
  order state machine with an explicit UNKNOWN state, a fail-closed order
  firewall, a kill switch and startup reconciliation; 11 test suites pass
  492 checks with 0 failures. The engine went through hundreds of hours of
  runs and observation across Binance Spot testnet, live market data and
  controlled real-capital scenarios. 504 pre-registered hypothesis cells
  across 8 study families (grids, cost models and decision rules fixed in
  advance; Bonferroni or Holm correction) yielded 0 net-positive candidates
  under retail Binance VIP 0 costs: gross moves of a few bps to about +20 bps
  at 5 s - 24 h horizons did not clear 10-30 bps round-trip costs and maker
  adverse selection. The engine was deliberately not moved to permanent live
  capital before its P0 safety closing gate was completed.
